University of Cambridge, Department of Materials Science and Metallurgy. Read the complete packages and their questions: [Semiconductors](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/semiconductors/index.php), [Dielectrics](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/dielectrics/index.php), [Ferroelectrics](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/ferroelectrics/index.php), [Ferromagnetism](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/ferromagnetic/index.php), [Piezoelectricity](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/piezoelectrics/index.php), [Pyroelectricity](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/pyroelectricity/index.php), [Thermal and electrical conduction](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/thermal_electrical/index.php) and [Thermal expansion](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/thermal-expansion/index.php).

Indexes and selected carrier, Fermi-level, junction, dielectric, magnetic-domain/anisotropy and poling pages were inspected directly on 30 October 2026. The intrinsic Fermi-level discussion implicitly needs symmetric effective densities of states for its exact mid-gap claim; derive the more general result in the linked learning Record. Treat simple refractive-index and loss comparisons with their frequency, constitutive and geometry assumptions. Not every interactive activity was exercised.

The inspected footer specifies CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 except where otherwise noted. Keep package and component credits. Readings and media remain external.

